{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"92c23781adbcc201","name":"card_event_desert_dust","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/BloodIron/events/card_event_desert_dust","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DESERT DUST","text":"Pin target unit. Add two GARRISON units to your support line.","flavorText":"Visual deception played a key role in Allied operations in North Africa during WWII. When Italy invaded Egypt in 1940, both sides faced the challenge of open desert terrain, leaving little natural cover. Camouflage and disguise became vital tools.In 1941, filmmaker Geoffrey Barkas was appointed Director of Camouflage at the British General Headquarters in Cairo. His team, which included artists and set designers, used creative tactics to mislead the enemy. One notable trick during the defense of Tobruk consisted in making an essential water purification building look bombed when it was undamaged. They also made airfields look damaged in order to fool reconnaissance aircraft flying over. As the deception proved effective, large-scale dummy equipment such as tanks, artillery, and soldiers were produced, along with fake railheads and pipelines. Sunshields, canvas covers that disguised tanks as trucks, were also developed. These techniques, especially at El Alamein, misled German forces into overestimating British strength and contributed to the Allied victory.","faction":"Britain","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_desert_dust","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_desert_dust_title","SourceString":"DESERT DUST","LocalizedString":"DESERT DUST"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_desert_dust_text","SourceString":"Pin target unit. Add two GARRISON units to your support line.","LocalizedString":"Pin target unit. Add two GARRISON units to your support line."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_desert_dust_history","SourceString":"Visual deception played a key role in Allied operations in North Africa during WWII. When Italy invaded Egypt in 1940, both sides faced the challenge of open desert terrain, leaving little natural cover. Camouflage and disguise became vital tools.In 1941, filmmaker Geoffrey Barkas was appointed Director of Camouflage at the British General Headquarters in Cairo. His team, which included artists and set designers, used creative tactics to mislead the enemy. One notable trick during the defense of Tobruk consisted in making an essential water purification building look bombed when it was undamaged. They also made airfields look damaged in order to fool reconnaissance aircraft flying over. As the deception proved effective, large-scale dummy equipment such as tanks, artillery, and soldiers were produced, along with fake railheads and pipelines. Sunshields, canvas covers that disguised tanks as trucks, were also developed. These techniques, especially at El Alamein, misled German forces into overestimating British strength and contributed to the Allied victory.","LocalizedString":"Visual deception played a key role in Allied operations in North Africa during WWII. When Italy invaded Egypt in 1940, both sides faced the challenge of open desert terrain, leaving little natural cover. Camouflage and disguise became vital tools.In 1941, filmmaker Geoffrey Barkas was appointed Director of Camouflage at the British General Headquarters in Cairo. His team, which included artists and set designers, used creative tactics to mislead the enemy. One notable trick during the defense of Tobruk consisted in making an essential water purification building look bombed when it was undamaged. They also made airfields look damaged in order to fool reconnaissance aircraft flying over. As the deception proved effective, large-scale dummy equipment such as tanks, artillery, and soldiers were produced, along with fake railheads and pipelines. Sunshields, canvas covers that disguised tanks as trucks, were also developed. These techniques, especially at El Alamein, misled German forces into overestimating British strength and contributed to the Allied victory."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Pin"],"spawnCardName":"card_unit_garrison","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'For_the_Queen'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/For_the_Queen.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Winter_2024/t_desert_dust.t_desert_dust","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Michael Turner","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/DESERT_DUST.DESERT_DUST","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":507.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_desert_dust_photo","SourceString":"A Crusader tank in the North African desert, masquerading as a truck in its “Sunshield”, 1942.","LocalizedString":"A Crusader tank in the North African desert, masquerading as a truck in its “Sunshield”, 1942."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[],"functions":[{"name":"CanPlayFromHand","owner":"card_event_desert_dust_C","params":[{"name":"canIt","type":"bool","direction":"out"},{"name":"reason","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam1","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"reasonParam2","type":"FString","direction":"out"},{"name":"targetedCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"out"}],"pure":false,"event":true,"flags":"FUNC_Event | FUNC_Public | FUNC_HasOutParms | FUNC_BlueprintCallable | FUNC_BlueprintEvent","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_hasTarget","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetTargetedCard_card","type":"UBaseCa